  ('niseko-japan', '08A', 'Niseko', 'Japan', 'The powder capital of the world', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Hokkaido', '{"adventure","culinary","expedition","family","romance","ski","ultra","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Powder capital of the world: ~15 m annual snowfall (JAPOW); Niseko-Shakotan-Otaru Kaigan Quasi-National Park, ~100 km south of Sapporo","Niseko United = four linked resorts (Annupuri, Grand HIRAFU, Niseko Village, Hanazono) on Mt Niseko Annupuri under one All Mountain Pass","Terrain: 50.8 km pistes (22.4 easy / 18.2 intermediate / 10.2 difficult), 32 lifts, base 255 m to 1,188 m, vertical 933 m","All Mountain Pass covers 29 lifts + gondolas, 60 runs + free inter-mountain shuttle; Mountain Collective member","Grand HIRAFU (biggest): 135 ha, 22 trails, 940 m vertical, longest run 5,300 m, 2 gondolas + 7 lifts; night skiing mid-Dec-late-Mar","Mt Yotei (Ezo Fuji) 1,898 m stratovolcano forces the storm moisture skyward - the reason the powder falls","Backcountry gate system pioneered in Japan (first gates 1999); 11 gates today; strict Niseko Rules; out-of-bounds rescue charged min JPY 100,000","Ultra-luxury tier: Park Hyatt Niseko Hanazono (100 rooms, 11 restaurants), Higashiyama Niseko Village Ritz-Carlton Reserve (50 rooms), Setsu Niseko (One Michelin Key); Michelin-starred Kamimura; deep onsen culture (Yukoro, Goshiki)"],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police / 119 fire + ambulance / #7119 medical advice (where available); ambulance dispatch free","hospital":"Kutchan (~10-15 min) for hospital services; Sapporo (~2 hrs) for major trauma; winter resort clinics","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"SERIOUS AVALANCHE COUNTRY: check Niseko Avalanche Information (niseko.nadare.info / nadare.jp JAN) daily; backcountry only via 11 designated gates with beacon/probe/shovel + guide; tree-well/deep-snow immersion suffocation risk (never ski trees alone); c